<article class="env-lemma" id="01JQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01JQ">Lemma <span data-tag="01JQ">26.17.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ and $g : Y \to S$ be morphisms of schemes with the same target. If $X, Y, S$ are all affine then $X \times _ S Y$ is affine. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose that $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$, $Y = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)$ and $S = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/01I4" data-tag="01I4">26.6.7</a> the affine scheme $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A \otimes _ R B)$ is the fibre product $X \times _ S Y$ in the category of locally ringed spaces. Hence it is a fortiori the fibre product in the category of schemes. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>